# House-style wording for Crisis 07 (#83). SPOILERS.
NOTE = "Embassy admin: last night's alliance note to Valde's office, drawn from your brief, went {route}. It read: \"{kj:%d}.\""
WREN = "From the liaison desk ({wren}): "
PS = "Political section: "
TEXT = {
 "briefing": {"dateLine": "The 26th. Late May.", "situation": [
   "Elsin's coalition government is in trouble. Prime Minister Henrik Valde governs with the Highlands Party, a rural party from the north led by Sanna Ekdal, and his majority is thin. Ekdal's voters are angry, and so are the crowds outside parliament.",
   "The opposition is led by Ruben Kask of National Renewal, who says Elsin should decide its own future \"without Kordav or the alliance.\" A government led by Kask would have to decide whether Task Force VEYL stays.",
   "Kordav's broadcaster is covering every hour of it.",
   "Each evening the alliance sends Valde's office a short note on Kordavan activity, drawn from your brief. Liaison requests go to Kalsa over LATTICE, unless the link is shut."]},
 "opening": {"text": "Valde's government is in trouble. Tell me whose doing it is.",
   "reassigned": "A new cell, and an old government in trouble. Tell me whose doing it is.",
   "byTone": {"good": "You were right about the link when nobody wanted you to be. Now Kalsa is unsteady, and everyone in my building has a theory. I would like yours.",
              "bad": "We got the last one wrong, and Kalsa remembers. This one is about Kalsa itself. Tell me whose business it is.",
              "warn": "Valde's government is in trouble. Tell me whose doing it is."}},
 "replies": {
   "handsoff": "I have said publicly that we will work with whichever government parliament chooses. Kask's office has asked for a meeting.",
   "handsoff_early": "I have said publicly that we will work with whichever government parliament chooses. Valde telephoned. He wanted to know when we had decided he was finished.",
   "channel": "The embassy has had a first, quiet conversation with Kask's foreign affairs adviser. Nothing was promised.",
   "postpone": "I have asked Valde to postpone the vote. He says he is considering it, which in Kalsa means yes.",
   "restraint": "The embassy has asked Elsin's police to show restraint.",
   "warnpub": "I have said publicly that Kordav is interfering in Elsin's politics. The press in Kalsa took a great interest.",
   "warnpriv": "The warning is in tonight's note to Valde. He says he will look into it.",
   "listen": "That gives me nothing to act on, and Kalsa is not waiting for us.",
   "stands": "That stands.",
   "postponed_next": "Valde postponed the vote. The organisers called it the alliance's decision, and twice as many people came out last night.",
   "backlash": "Kask spent the evening on television with my statement. He calls it \"the alliance choosing Elsin's government.\" The Courier agrees with him.",
   "overheard_ksb": "Kordav's broadcaster led its news with it: \"The alliance whispers to Valde that his opponents are Kordav's.\" It quoted the note.",
   "overheard_police": "On our warning, Valde's police questioned two of the organisers last night. The organisers have gone to the Courier."},
 "triggers": {
   "early": "Credibility −1. Valde wanted to know when the alliance had decided he was finished.",
   "hedging": "Credibility −1. Low again. \"Kalsa is not waiting for us.\""},
 "sources": {"S-HERON": "A staffer in the Highlands Party. She sees the party's meetings and drafts. New. Don't task her two days running."},
 "items": {
   "R-1-01": PS + "the Highlands Party has given Valde a week. It wants a public inquiry into {grievance}, or it leaves the coalition.\nEkdal told our political officer she \"has not decided anything, and has not been asked to by anyone.\"\n{majority} {vell}",
   "R-1-02": "Kalsa: about 3,000 people protested outside parliament this afternoon over {grievance}. The protest was peaceful. Many came in by bus from the north.",
   "R-1-03": "Kordav's state broadcaster: \"Elsin's people tire of foreign soldiers, and of foreign winters.\"",
   "R-1-04": WREN + "\"Kordav's embassy in Kalsa has doubled its press staff this month and is buying advertising on Elsin's news sites.\"\nSourcing: the service's own observation.",
   "R-1-05": "Embassy admin: Elsin's Ministry of Finance and Economy, which was the Ministry of Finance until last year, regrets that its new letterhead is still delayed. Correspondence on the old paper remains valid until stocks run out.",
   "R-2-01": PS + "Kask and Ekdal met last night, for the first time in two years. Both say it was about farm subsidies.",
   "R-2-02": "Kalsa: about 12,000 protesters today, with tractors from the north. A window was broken at the agriculture ministry. Police made four arrests.",
   "R-2-03": "A \"leaked bank document\" is circulating widely. On the letterhead of Elsin's Ministry of Finance, it records a transfer of 2 million from a Kordavan \"Agrarian Fund\" to National Renewal.\nUnverified.",
   "R-2-04": "Kalsa Evening Courier, interview with Kask: \"Elsin's future will be decided in Elsin. Not in Kordav, and not by the alliance.\"",
   "R-2-05": NOTE % 1, "R-3-05": NOTE % 2, "R-4-05": NOTE % 3, "R-5-04": NOTE % 4,
   "R-2-06": PS + "a source close to Valde's office tells our embassy, unprompted, that {claim:1}.",
   "R-2-07": PS + "a source close to Valde's office says the alliance \"has it wrong.\" He says Kordav's money is behind the Highlands Party, and that Ekdal has been bought.",
   "R-3-01": PS + "at noon Ekdal took the Highlands Party out of the coalition. A motion of no confidence has been tabled for the morning of the 31st.",
   "R-3-02": "Kalsa: the largest protest yet, about 40,000. Police used water cannon near parliament. Thirty people were hurt, two of them police officers.",
   "R-3-03": "Kordav's state broadcaster: \"The alliance's man Valde turns water cannon on his own farmers.\"",
   "R-3-04": WREN + "\"Two of the protest's organisers took part in a Kordav-funded youth exchange ten years ago.\"\nSourcing: old exchange records.",
   "R-3-06": PS + "the same source close to Valde's office says that {claim:2}, and that this is \"what everyone in the prime minister's office believes.\"",
   "R-3-07": PS + "the same source says Ekdal's press conference \"was written in Kordav's embassy.\"",
   "R-4-01": PS + "Valde will not resign, and will face the vote. Kask and Ekdal are close to a deal. Her price is the inquiry and the agriculture ministry.",
   "R-4-02": "Photos posted overnight claim to show the protest organisers \"at a Kordavan training camp.\"\nThe men in the photos are in winter coats, and there is snow on the ground behind them.",
   "R-4-03": "Kalsa Evening Courier, poll: 58% want a new government. 61% want Task Force VEYL to stay.",
   "R-4-04": "Embassy admin: the air conditioning has failed in the heat. Kalsa reached 29°C today. Staff may remove their ties.",
   "R-4-06": PS + "the same source repeats that {claim:3}, and adds that \"the alliance should say so before it's too late.\"",
   "R-4-07": PS + "the same source says Kordavan money is paying for the protesters' buses.",
   "R-5-01": PS + "Kask and Ekdal have signed a coalition agreement. Kask, at the signing: \"We will review the task force agreement. Review, not end.\"",
   "R-5-02": "Kordav's state broadcaster: \"Tomorrow Elsin chooses: sovereignty, or occupation.\"",
   "R-5-03": "Kalsa: the protest organisers have called off tomorrow's march \"to let parliament decide.\"",
   "R-5-05": PS + "the same source repeats that {claim:4}, and says the prime minister \"is waiting for the alliance to speak.\"",
   "R-5-06": PS + "the same source says Kask will expel the task force within a month of taking office.",
   "C-01": "Source reports: Ekdal decided after three weeks of meetings in her own constituency, where nobody has forgiven anyone. She dislikes Kask, and says she will vote against Valde anyway.\nAccess: direct. She sat in on the meetings.",
   "C-02": "Source reports: Ekdal's deal with Kask is the inquiry, the agriculture ministry, and a promise not to touch the task force for a year. Nothing in it mentions Kordav or money.\nAccess: direct. She has seen the draft.",
   "C-03": "Open sources, on the protests' funding: small donations, a farmers' union and a transport union pay for the buses. One account linked to a Kordavan grain trader gave about a thousandth of the total.",
   "C-04": "Open sources, on the bank document: the letterhead uses the ministry's old name, dropped last year, and an account-number format that Elsin's banks don't use. The document was first posted by an account created on the 26th.",
   "C-05": "Bureau traffic, an instruction to its Kalsa team: \"Amplify. Don't touch the vote; it will fall on its own. What we need is the alliance saying the word Kordav in public.\"",
   "C-06": "Open sources, on National Renewal's finances: its donors are mostly Elsin businessmen. One is a grain importer who trades with Kordav. Everything is declared.",
   "C-07": "In answer to our request, Elsin's security service: the organisers are local, a farmers' union and a students' group. No foreign links found.",
   "C-07K": "Kordav's state broadcaster, in passing: \"Valde's police now investigate peaceful farmers at the alliance's request.\"",
   "C-08": "Open sources, on the numbers in parliament: with the Highlands Party, Valde survives any motion. Without it, a motion passes."},
 "notes": {
   ("marrow", "R-1-02"): "Three thousand people on a weekday is real anger. Nobody gets paid enough to stand in the rain for that.",
   ("vasko", "R-1-04"): "Doubling the press staff. I've seen Kordav do that before, and it's how these things start.",
   ("vasko", "R-2-03"): "And there is the money.",
   ("marrow", "R-2-04"): "Kask is against everybody. Kordav won't enjoy him as much as it thinks.",
   ("halden", "R-2-03"): "The letterhead says Ministry of Finance. The ministry changed its name last year.",
   ("vasko", "R-3-04"): "Ten years ago. They plan a long way ahead.",
   ("marrow", "R-3-04"): "A youth exchange ten years ago is a youth exchange. It isn't a recruitment.",
   ("vasko", "R-4-03"): "I don't trust a poll taken in the middle of a crisis.",
   ("marrow", "R-4-03"): "Sixty-one percent want the task force to stay. That's the figure I'd look at.",
   ("halden", "R-4-02"): "There is snow on the ground in that photo. It's May, and it was 29 degrees yesterday.",
   ("vasko", "R-5-03"): "If they're calling off the march, they think they've already won in parliament."},
 "analysts": {
   "vasko": "He settles on a reading early. After the damage assessment he saw Kordav in everything. He was right once, about the cancelled march.",
   "halden": "Careful, and slow. She wasn't wrong once. The letterhead and the snow each reached you a day late.",
   "marrow": "She reads crowds and polls well, and was right every time. Her best scenario."},
 "lessons": [
   "Some crises are not the adversary's doing. Ekdal left the coalition over her own voters' grievance.",
   "An adversary can want to be accused. Ask who gains from your statement as well as from the event.",
   "Your own assessment, quoted back by someone who shouldn't have read it, is a leak. It isn't corroboration.",
   "A government can fall without the country changing sides. In the Courier's poll, 61% wanted the task force to stay.",
   "Staying out of it still takes work. The best outcome needed a channel to the opposition before the vote."],
}
